4. Quality Control Initiation
Submission of the Goods Receipt form initiates the quality-control process for the received raw materials
and packing materials.
The quality process follows this sequence:
1. COA Number Generation
2. Sample Advice Generation
3. RM/PM COA Generation
4. COA Number Generation
The first step is the generation of a Certificate of Analysis (COA) number for the received material.
Each raw material and packing material has a predefined testing template configured within the RMBM
system. After the COA number is generated, the relevant product-specific template becomes available to
the Quality Executive or Quality Officer.
The responsible quality user completes the required test details in the relevant form.
6. Sample Advice Generation
After the initial quality form is completed, the entry moves to Sample Advice Generation.
The Sample Advice is generated for the received material and records the material submitted for quality
testing.
7. RM/PM COA Generation
Once the Sample Advice process is completed, the entry moves to RM/PM COA Generation.
At this stage, the final Certificate of Analysis for the Raw Material / Packing Material is generated,
completing the defined quality process for the incoming material.
8. Billing Module Update
After the material is physically received at the facility and the Goods Receipt form is submitted, the
corresponding entry also appears under Incoming Bills in the Billing module.
